{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379779-uminchu-the-unending-scales-peach","id":1379779,"title":"Uminchu, The Unending Scales [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-09T09:21:11-07:00","id":1379779,"title":"Uminchu, The Unending Scales [PEACH]","content":"So, one of my players wanted an artifact that would help with being a war leader and I felt like sharing, Here's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12dmBeh6R10_Oh8BG7jEXlhJK3PWJvQONyxqwV88b5E0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Uminchu, The Unending Scales</a>. Let me know what you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T09:45:28-07:00","id":1379783,"title":"","content":"I don't have a good handle on game balance, but this is really cool and brutal. It...certainly says a lot about the kind of warleader who would use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:40:52-07:00","id":1379803,"title":"","content":"Pretty interesting. Heres a couple of my notes.<br /> <br /> One Through Blood: The costs are a little unclear, you mean normally it is 1 mote to activate for your Circle or ally? That's too cheap. Or do you mean it always cost a 1lhl and the more additions is for a battle group? And what do you mean by the affected characters ending the wearers commitment. The only mention of commitment is for the armor proper? So basically confused in the pricing and cost for the wielder basically.<br /> <br /> Salt-Slicked Scales&amp;Hook Fang Jaws: Hm, unsure having these powers be permanent additions. I would look into how Lunars handle mutations it but since I haven't backed it Its mainly a concern that I have. Unsure how it looks in practice.<br /> <br /> Blood in the Water: One, it's a Essence 1 charm but to activate it One Through Blood has to be Essence 2. Probably should raise its Essence then. Also Non-Charm successes are very powerful. I would say probably should raise the cost of the Evocation since at 2m it be a bit broken.<br /> <br /> Feeding Frenzy Call: this is better, mainly since it's both dice and its fully limited by wound penalty. So either 1, 2, or 4. That's seems reasonable for me. Cost is a bit low but it is also more limited so it works.<br /> <br /> Tear to Pieces: Hm, doubling Onslaught penalties. That's very powerful. I can't think of any parallels it would have in the Splat charm trees off the top of my so I can't gauge how balanced it is currently, hm.<br /> <br /> Fearless Hungry Maw: Perfect Morale is very strong, but I think the restrictions makes it works. That's just how I think anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T10:55:20-07:00","id":1380157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379779-uminchu-the-unending-scales-peach?p=1379803#post1379803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty interesting. Heres a couple of my notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One Through Blood: The costs are a little unclear, you mean normally it is 1 mote to activate for your Circle or ally? That's too cheap. Or do you mean it always cost a 1lhl and the more additions is for a battle group? And what do you mean by the affected characters ending the wearers commitment. The only mention of commitment is for the armor proper? So basically confused in the pricing and cost for the wielder basically. </div> </div> </div>It always costs a health level to activate. The Charm is indefinite, meaning that the effect lasts for as long as the character continues to commit Essence to it, but I put in an escape clause for someone who decides that they no longer want to have fish mutations and I wanted to make it clear that the character stops committing Essence to maintain the effect for a given character as soon as that character opts out. I've cleaned up the cost and text a bit. Hopefully that helps.<br /> <br /> How much Essence do you think the Charm should cost, given that it requires the wearer to maintain an ongoing commitment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Salt-Slicked Scales&amp;Hook Fang Jaws: Hm, unsure having these powers be permanent additions. I would look into how Lunars handle mutations it but since I haven't backed it Its mainly a concern that I have. Unsure how it looks in practice. </div> </div> </div>Permanent changes made the most sense as these Charm effects are farmed out to members of the shoal through One Through Blood. If they had an activation cost, then how would mortals pay that activation cost?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood in the Water: One, it's a Essence 1 charm but to activate it One Through Blood has to be Essence 2. Probably should raise its Essence then. Also Non-Charm successes are very powerful. I would say probably should raise the cost of the Evocation since at 2m it be a bit broken. </div> </div> </div>You have a good point on the Essence requirement, though there is technically the option to induct ~10 individuals and making them into a battle group. Because you can only make a single successful Rally For Numbers for a given battle group once (until they drop in Size), I figured non-Charm successes would be fine, though you are right that the cost is cheap. I'll move it up to 4 motes, since the most likely number of successes it will add is two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tear to Pieces: Hm, doubling Onslaught penalties. That's very powerful. I can't think of any parallels it would have in the Splat charm trees off the top of my so I can't gauge how balanced it is currently, hm. </div> </div> </div>I've considered making Tear To Pieces into the capstone Charm instead of Fearless Hungry Maws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:40:32-07:00","id":1380195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379779-uminchu-the-unending-scales-peach?p=1380157#post1380157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always costs a health level to activate. The Charm is indefinite, meaning that the effect lasts for as long as the character continues to commit Essence to it, but I put in an escape clause for someone who decides that they no longer want to have fish mutations and I wanted to make it clear that the character stops committing Essence to maintain the effect for a given character as soon as that character opts out. I've cleaned up the cost and text a bit. Hopefully that helps.<br /> <br /> How much Essence do you think the Charm should cost, given that it requires the wearer to maintain an ongoing commitment?</div> </div> </div> </div>With it being a commitment, I would say its already a fair price. I was just confused since I didn't know whether the heath level was always necessary or only for battle groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Permanent changes made the most sense as these Charm effects are farmed out to members of the shoal through One Through Blood. If they had an activation cost, then how would mortals pay that activation cost? </div> </div> </div>True. Hm, I would say to allow others to use the other mutations, raise the commitment by one maybe? If that's to expensive for the Exalt then probably keep it as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have a good point on the Essence requirement, though there is technically the option to induct ~10 individuals and making them into a battle group. Because you can only make a single successful Rally For Numbers for a given battle group once (until they drop in Size), I figured non-Charm successes would be fine, though you are right that the cost is cheap. I'll move it up to 4 motes, since the most likely number of successes it will add is two. </div> </div> </div>I would say at the point you are inducting10 people individually it be to much, since by that point you are commiting about 10 motes or so. So it probably make sense to just raise the Essence. Everything else seems good though. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}